    "narrative": "Our offensive core is anchored by **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (75.05) and **Lawrence Butler** (70.87), both of whom present as the strongest plays on today's board. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** benefits from a high-leverage spot in the #2 hole against Walbert Ure\u00f1a; despite the catcher's arm potentially shaving a fraction of a point, his overall command of the strike zone and the favorable SP_xERA environment make him an elite start. **Lawrence Butler** is poised for a significant output against Taj Bradley, bolstered by a strong park factor and a substantial +13% dynamic platoon edge. While **Jonathan Aranda** (65.40) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (63.50) trail slightly in total score, both are high-conviction plays today, benefiting significantly from favorable matchups against Jackson Jobe and Brady Singer, respectively.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the rotation involved **Justin Crawford**, whose score of 50.49 left him on the outside looking in. While his sprint speed typically makes him a priority, his projected #9 spot in the order against a formidable arm like George Kirby dragged his efficiency below our current starters. We are prioritizing the higher-ordered bats like **Bryce Harper** (62.31) and **Daulton Varsho** (60.50) to ensure we maximize our run-scoring potential, even at the cost of some stolen base upside. We remain wary of the volatility surrounding **Cal Raleigh** (48.97) and **Yainer Diaz** (53.30); with both lineups currently pending, their scores are susceptible to shift if they are dropped in the batting order. Additionally, **Gleyber Torres** faces a tricky outing against Ian Seymour; while the platoon advantage is favorable, his score is depressed by a difficult SP_xERA, requiring a sharp performance to avoid burning one of our daily game caps.",
